/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  batch13_nacl_pitzer / constant/crystallisation

  Kinetics in the SAME form as every other crystalliser in the corpus:
      growth      G  = k_g (S-1)^g            [m/s]
      nucleation  B0 = k_b (S-1)^b M_T^j      [#/(m^3 s)]

  j = 0 (primary) so the unseeded charge bootstraps from S > 1.

  ILLUSTRATIVE constants, and labelled as such: NaCl growth and nucleation
  rates are strongly impurity- and hydrodynamics-dependent, and this case
  exists to show WHERE the supersaturation comes from, not to publish a rate.
  The thermodynamics (Pitzer, curated) is the part that is real here.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

naclBatchKinetics
{
    growth
    {
        k_g   2.0e-8;     // m/s        (illustrative)
        g     1.0;
    }
    nucleation
    {
        k_b   5.0e8;      // #/(m^3 s)  (illustrative)
        b     2.0;
        j     0.0;        // primary nucleation (unseeded bootstrap)
    }
}
